{"tool_name":"umi-tools","contents":["galaxy","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"umi-tools","home":"https://github.com/CGATOxford/UMI-tools","license":"MIT","summary":"Tools for handling Unique Molecular Identifiers in NGS data sets.","addition_date":"2018-08-10T12:43:22Z","last_update_date":"2018-12-10T12:59:01Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:umi-tools","credit":[{"email":"i.sudbery@sheffield.ac.uk","name":"Ian Sudbery","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://github.com/CGATOxford/UMI-tools"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Sequencing quality control","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3218"}]}],"name":"UMI-tools","operating_system":["Linux"],"owner":"d.gabrielaitis","publication":[{"doi":"10.1101/gr.209601.116","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2017 Smith et al.Unique Molecular Identifiers (UMIs) are random oligonucleotide barcodes that are increasingly used in high-throughput sequencing experiments. Through a UMI, identical copies arising from distinct molecules can be distinguished from those arising through PCR amplification of the same molecule. However, bioinformatic methods to leverage the information from UMIs have yet to be formalized. In particular, sequencing errors in the UMI sequence are often ignored or else resolved in an ad hoc manner. We show that errors in the UMI sequence are common and introduce network-based methods to account for these errors when identifying PCR duplicates. Using these methods, we demonstrate improved quantification accuracy both under simulated conditions and real iCLIP and single-cell RNA-seq data sets. Reproducibility between iCLIP replicates and single-cell RNA-seq clustering are both improved using our proposed network-based method, demonstrating the value of properly accounting for errors in UMIs. These methods are implemented in the open source UMI-tools software package.","authors":[{"name":"Heger A."},{"name":"Smith T."},{"name":"Sudbery I."}],"citationCount":309,"date":"2017-03-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Genome Research","title":"UMI-tools: Modeling sequencing errors in Unique Molecular Identifiers to improve quantification accuracy"},"pmcid":"PMC5340976","pmid":"28100584"}],"topic":[{"term":"NGS","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3168"},{"term":"Quality affairs","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3393"},{"term":"Sequence sites, features and motifs","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0160"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"UMI-tools","home":"https://bio.tools/umi-tools","license":"MIT","summary":"Tools for handling Unique Molecular Identifiers in NGS data sets.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"galaxy":{"version":"1.1.6","first_commit":"2017-08-09","conda_name":"umi_tools","conda_version":"1.1.6","summary":"UMI-tools extract - Extract UMIs from fastq","edam_operations":["Sequencing quality control"],"edam_topics":["NGS","Sequence sites, features and motifs","Quality affairs"],"toolshed_categories":["Sequence Analysis","Transcriptomics","Single Cell"],"toolshed_id":"umi-tools","users_5_years":1319,"users_all_time":1470,"usage_5_years":78834,"usage_all_time":105057,"bio_tools_summary":"Tools for handling Unique Molecular Identifiers in NGS data sets.","bio_tools_ids":"umi-tools","bio_tools_name":"UMI-tools","related_tutorials":["https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/single-cell/tutorials/scrna-preprocessing/tutorial.html","https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/single-cell/tutorials/scrna-umis/tutorial.html","https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/transcriptomics/tutorials/clipseq/tutorial.html"],"related_workflows":[{"create_time":"2025-06-02","latest_version":"1","link":"https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/1706?version=1","name":"Tutorial CLIPseq Explorer Demultiplexed PEAKachu eCLIP Hg38"},{"create_time":"2025-06-02","latest_ve